  "register": "notes",
  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nAugmentin / Spiriva with HandiHaler / ciprofloxacin / Bactrim\n\nChief Complaint:\nMalaise, cough\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ with h/o tracheobroncheomalacia s/p tracheobronchoplasty in \n___, now with mesh erosion s/p repeat bronchoscopy between \n___ and ___, COPD, now presents with SOB x 2 days.  \nPt reports worsening SOB over the last 2 days with chest \ncongestion. She has a chronic productive cough but reports it is \nmore dry and she has trouble getting up secretions over the last \ncouple of days. When she gets up sputum, it is sparse and \nyellow-green. She had a low-grade fever to 100 approx 1wk ago \nand intermitent chills since. Mild malaise. Occasional chest \npain that has been ongoing. She reports taking the Cipro/Bactrim \nfor approx ___ after discharge in ___ but stopped because she \nfelt they made her fatigued and sick. She is not currently on \nany ABX. She reports she feels she has an ongoing lung/airway \ninfection. No wheezing. She has lost 15lbs in the last few weeks \nto months.  \nPt admitted ___ bronch done during admission. Pt seen by \nID. Put on IV cefepime and then PO Cipro and Bactrim as \nsuppressive therapy. Pt seen in ___ clinic today and sent in for \nadmission and IV ABX before considering repeat bronch.  \n \nIn the ED, initial vitals were: 98.9 80 146/79 18 100% ra  \n- Exam: Afebrile, HDS, 100% RA. Cardiac normal. RLL rhonchi, \nfaint b/l crackles. Abd normal. No peripheral edema  \n- Labs were significant for: WBC 7.8, Hb 11, normal lytes with K \nof 3, lactate 1.1  \n- Imaging revealed: CXR negative  \n- The patient was given: Vanc/cefepime, PO K  \n- ___ y/o F with recurrent PNA, TBM, found to grow pseudo on \nbronchoscopy ___, here with dyspnea and cough, RLL rhonchi on \nexam. CXR negative for obvious infiltrate, but patient known to \nhave grown pseudomonas on bronchoscopy cultures, also having \ndifficulty managing worsening secretions given obstruction from \nmesh erosion. Will require inpatient admission for antibiotics \nand management of secretions. Interventional pulmonology will \nconsult.  \n \nUpon arrival to the floor, pt is without complaints other than \nsame SOB that brought her in.  \nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS:  \n(+) Per HPI  \nDenies n/v/d, dysuria, no hx of malignancy, no recent \nimmobilization or surgery\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nTracheobronchomalacia\nTrachebronchitis",
